lunduke-edit (0.9-11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace All no longer erases the open document a slice at a time.
    The new text is built in a detached buffer, in slices bounded by
    wall-clock time, then swapped in as one undo step. Highlighting,
    bracket matching, and search highlighting stay off during that
    swap. The title drops "Replacing… 100%" when the commit ends, so
    it is not still showing while the result dialog is open.
  * Opening a large file stores heights for one screen before
    GtkSourceView paints, so the main loop keeps handling Escape and
    moving the window until the file is fully open. A full-buffer
    line walk on the first draw no longer runs.
  * Replace All shows progress while it counts matches. A large commit
    is erased and inserted in short slices and remains one undo step.
    Cancel and Escape work through that commit.
  * The line-number gutter numbers the empty line after a final newline.
  * A production-binary test measures main-loop stalls with X11
    _NET_WM_PING, including under cpulimit -l 25.
  * Respin: a taller window, or one resized during open or Replace All,
    measures the pixel-cache margin as well as the first allocation.
    A paint no longer walks every line of a 12 MB buffer.
  * Opening a file inserts text, applies the font tag, and records
    line endings in short slices, including a file of several million
    short lines. Escape during that work is not dropped. The previous
    document is cleared in short slices first, and a file that is not
    valid UTF-8 still opens as Latin-1.
  * Replace All keeps "Replacing… N%" and the previous size on screen
    until the new text is swapped in, and asks about a very large undo
    record before the counting pass.
  * Undo of a large Replace All restores the previous text in short
    slices, so that one step does not freeze the main loop.
  * Cancelling Replace All — from the large-undo question, before the
    swap, or during the swap — leaves the buffer unmodified and does
    not mark it dirty. The stall test delivers Escape to the Find
    window only after that swap has started.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

lunduke-edit (0.9-10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace All builds the new text off the buffer in short main-loop
    slices, with a Replacing progress line. Cancel and Escape leave the
    buffer unchanged. The commit is one undo step.
  * Opening a large file measures one screen before the first paint, so
    the window stays responsive and the Opening percentage advances.
    Escape during that paint still restores the previous text.
  * The line and column in the status bar follow typing, undo, paste,
    and Replace.
  * Ctrl+End keeps scrolling until the caret is on screen, including
    while line heights are still being measured.
  * The throttled open test requires cpulimit -l 25 and fails if the
    limit cannot be applied.

