lunduke-edit (0.9-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A file that contains a null byte is refused, and the buffer that was
    already open is left in place. Open failures for a permission error,
    a missing path, and a directory name the reason as well as the path.
    Cancelling the question for a file larger than 32 MiB is not followed
    by an error. The 64 MiB ceiling is still a refusal.
  * Middle-click inserts the primary selection once, at the pointer. A
    click outside the selection leaves that selection in place.
  * Inserting or deleting a line in a mixed-ending file keeps the other
    lines' endings, including across undo. The status byte count adds a
    CR only for lines that will be written as CRLF.
  * Closing Find drops the hidden Search Selection Only range and the
    extend anchor. Find Next pins the selection that is on screen, and
    says so when nothing is selected.
  * Print measures each source line. A line that wraps to more than one
    visual row is paginated with the tabbed-line path.
  * The dialog for a file that changed on disk offers Reload. Opening the
    path this window already has re-reads it when the inode or mtime
    changed, and asks first when the buffer is dirty.
  * Text → Show Line Numbers uses Alt+N, so it no longer shares Alt+L
    with Latin-1.

