lunduke-edit (0.8-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A failed save stays unsaved and no longer truncates the file. The new
    bytes are written to a temporary file and replace the original only
    after the write succeeds.
  * Save As writes the path that was confirmed. It does not change the
    extension after the overwrite prompt, so notes.txt.txt is not saved as
    notes.txt and a name like report does not silently replace report.txt.
  * Opening a file that is not UTF-8 keeps the detected Latin-1 encoding.
    A save with no edits no longer rewrites those bytes as UTF-8.
  * Opening a file from a second launch or a file manager asks before
    dropping unsaved edits. Every file named on the command line is opened.
  * A short or failed read is not treated as the whole file.
  * Printing no longer clips the top of the first line on each page.
  * Line numbers scroll with the text.
  * File → Exit quits the application.
  * One Replace is a single undo step. Find Next no longer skips a
    character, so both letters in "xx" can be replaced, and Wrap Around
    does not jump to an earlier match because of that skip.
  * Start at Top applies to that search and then turns off. Search
    Selection Only does nothing when nothing is selected. Replace still
    replaces the match when Extend Selection has grown the selection.
  * Undoing back to the saved text clears the unsaved marker.
  * Go to Line rejects trailing junk such as 12abc. The column readout
    counts tab stops using the tab width.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 16:40:00 -0500

